        tox c -e test -k extras -x testenv.extras=blue
 
+Substitutions inside an override
+================================
+
+.. versionadded:: 4.61
+
+An override value goes through the same substitution pass as a value in the configuration file. For example:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+   tox -x env_run_base.commands='pytest {posargs:tests}' -e py -- -k slow
+
+runs ``pytest -k slow``: ``{posargs:tests}`` is replaced with the positional arguments passed after ``--``, falling
+back to ``tests`` when none are given.
+
+.. note::
+
+   Overrides use the ini spelling of a substitution even in a TOML project, so ``{posargs}``, ``{env:VAR}`` and
+   ``{env_name}`` keep working the same way whatever the configuration file format.
+
 Escaping dots in override keys
 ==============================
 
